# RTU API is read-only

Call the RTU SOAP API only to read. A write is allowed only when a separate task names that exact operation. Settings, an access check, a bugfix, or write bits on the role do not allow a write.

`POST` is the SOAP transport. It is not a mutation. This service may send one read: `getObjects` (`table` and `procedure`) from Settings → «Проверить доступ».

Do not add `getObjectId`, `getLookup`, `describeObject`, `describeTable`, `describeProcedure`, `describeProcedureContext`, `selectRowset`, or `countRowset` unless a task asks for that specific read.

Do not send `insertRowset`, `updateRowset`, `deleteRowset`, `transaction`, `checkRowset`, `call`, `callContext`, API v1, the `args:node` header, or the `http://mfisoft.ru/auth` namespace. `checkRowset` is a write: its actions are `insert`, `update`, and `delete`.

The operation name is the literal `getObjects` in the envelope builder. Do not accept an operation name from a caller, a flag, or the WSDL. Ignore write operations that appear in the WSDL.

Do not invent object names. Do not send headers or bodies that are not in the 2.0 handbook or the live WSDL v2. Do not log the SOAP envelope. The password stays ciphertext at rest and is sent only on the pinned HTTPS host.
